<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div><strong>Processive verbs</strong></div>
    <div><strong>Present tense</strong></div>
    <div>verb-<strong>nŭn/(ŭ)n</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">는/(은)ㄴ</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">가는</div>
    <div class="col">ka-nŭn</div>
    <div class="col">going</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">먹는</div>
    <div class="col">mŏk-nŭn => mŏngnŭn</div>
    <div class="col">eating</div>
    <div><strong>Past tense</strong></div>
    <div>verb-<strong>(ŭ)n</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">(은)ㄴ</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">간</div>
    <div class="col">ka-n</div>
    <div class="col">was going</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">먹은</div>
    <div class="col">mŏk-ŭn => mŏgŭn</div>
    <div class="col">was eating</div>
</div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div><strong>Descriptive verbs</strong></div>
    <div>verb-<strong>(ŭ)n</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">(은)ㄴ</div>
</div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div><strong>Act of doing (verb)-ing</strong></div>
    <div>verb <strong>kŏt/kŏ</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">것/거</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">가는 것</div>
    <div class="col">kanŭn kŏt</div>
    <div class="col">act of going</div>
</div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div><strong>It seems like (verb)-ing</strong></div>
    <div>verb <strong>kŏt kat'ayo</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">것 같아요</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">사람이 빵을 <span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">먹는 것 같아요</span></div>
    <div>saram-i ppang-ŭl mŏngnŭn kŏt kat'ayo</div>
    <div>person-[subject] bread-[object] eating-[seems like]</div>
    <div>It seems like the person is eating bread</div>
</div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div><strong>Future, will (verb)</strong></div>
    <div>verb-<strong>(ŭ)l</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">(을)ㄹ</div>
</div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div><strong>It seems like will be (verb)-ing</strong></div>
    <div>verb-<strong>(ŭ)l kŏt kat'ayo</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">을 것 같아요</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">사람이 빵을 <span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">먹을 것 같아요</span></div>
    <div>saram-i ppang-ŭl mŏgŭl kŏt kat'ayo</div>
    <div>person-[subject] bread-[object] eating-[seems like will]</div>
    <div>It seems like the person will be eating bread</div>
</div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div><strong>When (verb)-ing</strong></div>
    <div>verb-<strong>(ŭ)l ttae</strong></div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">을 때</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">학교에 <span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">갈 때</span></div>
    <div>hakkyo-e ka-l ttae</div>
    <div>school-to go-[when]</div>
    <div>When I go to school</div>
</div>
<div class="row grammar-cell">
    <div><strong>Adjectival clause</strong></div>
    <div>modifier + noun</div>
    <div class="grammar-verbs-ideograms small">제가 <span class="grammar-verbs-highlight">멍는</span> 사과가 썩었어요</div>
    <div>che-ga mŏng-nŭn sagwa-ga ssŏgŏssŏyo</div>
    <div>I-[subject] eating apple-[subject] gone off [polite past]</div>
    <div>The apple that I am eating has gone off</div>
</div>
